## Detail Page — Design Tab Content, Standard Brief (wireframe review, 17 Jul 2026 — provisional, see note above)

**C&CM's equivalent (different structure — per-region/customer nesting) is confirmed deferred** until the Standard layout is fully locked.

**Top of page:** Project Name and Assigned Lead Designers, visually tidied, same functionality as today.

**Section navigation — supersedes the earlier in-card tab-toggle.** The Design tab splits into three full sections switched from the project sidebar rail: **Project Details**, **Deliverables**, **Submissions**.

**Project Details section** — four cards: Project Name card (Job Number, Project Status, Add Secondary CS, CS Lead, Secondary CS), Designer Assignments card (Team/Designer/Action table), Brief Overview card (Client Name, Initial/Final Deadline, Client Expectation/What to Avoid/Additional Information), Reference Files card (drag-and-drop anywhere on the card, one row per file with Preview/Download/Delete — Delete restricted to CS/Admin/Management).

**Deliverables section** — its own full rail-selected section. List, one row per deliverable: Deliverable Name (left), 2D/3D/Technical team tags → Deadline → Files → Status (right, **confirmed column order: Deadline → Files → Status**). Header row: count indicator + Focused/All toggle.

**Submissions section** — see "Detail Page — Submission Section" below.

**Default section on entering Design:** first-ever visit to a given project's Detail page defaults to Project Details; every subsequent visit defaults to Deliverables. **Implementation dependency:** needs a "has this user viewed this project's Detail page before" marker (see the new table in the Code Architecture section below).

**Team-tag click-to-assignment-mode:**
- Tags populate only for teams actually requested for that deliverable.
- Clicking an unassigned tag expands it into inline assignment mode (designers self-assign, team leads assign anyone on their team).
- Once assigned, becomes an avatar + name + team chip.
- **Reassignable**, gated behind a confirmation step (reassigning someone off a deliverable they may already be working on shouldn't be a single misclick).
- **Visual affordance:** unassigned tags get a static dashed-border + "+" cue at rest, not just hover.

**Files Button** — opens that deliverable's NAS working-files folder. Distinct from Reference Files (Project Details) and the Projects-page row-expansion sub-table (glance-and-move-on summary, not the interactive working surface this is).

**Deliverables Focused/All toggle:** default Focused. Focused shows only deliverables where the viewer's own team is requested, regardless of assignment. Scope: team-scoped roles only (Designer, Team Lead) — CS/Management/Admin always see the equivalent of All.

**Naming convention:** "Initial Deadline" / "Final Deadline" consistently across all pages (already applied on the Projects page).

