## Briefing / Create Page Architecture (locked 17 Jul 2026 — still provisional, see note below)

**Scope: visual overhaul only, no structural rework.** The page's actual structure isn't the problem — it just looks like "admin work." No hooks/placeholders for Finance/Production/Logistics needed here.

**C&CM Details wireframe** — two cards: Concept & KV card (Requirements, Deadline Date/Time, Options Required — numbers-only field), Regions & Customers card (UAE flat list; Gulf requires selecting a country first via toggle buttons, then customers within it — **selection persists across toggling**).

**"Losing track" concern — resolved, two combined fixes:** a persistent "Selected Customers" chip strip at the bottom of the Regions & Customers card (grouped by region/country, removable chips), plus a count badge on each Gulf country toggle button.

**C&CM Deliverables section:** each region gets a collapsible header; within it, every customer gets its own div reusing the exact same Deliverables Edit-mode structure locked for Standard.

**Drafts stays a separate page, NOT folded into the Projects page.** `/projects/drafts` is a deliberate safe landing point before Create — separate from the Projects table's saved views, not an oversight to consolidate.

**Top of page:** sticky top bar with a Current Brief Type toggle (C&CM / Standard), always visible. Toggling brief type only changes the Deliverables section — Project Basics, Teams & Deadline, Reference Files are shared fields. Three cards: Project Basics, Teams & Deadline, Reference Files.

**Naming fixed:** "First Submission Deadline" → "Initial Deadline."

**"Generate FOC Number"** — existing, proven functionality, reused as-is.

**"Design Teams Required" checkboxes** — existing functionality, carried over. **Still open:** whether this project-level team selection also restricts which teams a deliverable can request — worth direct confirmation.

**Brief Details + Deliverables section:**
- Brief Details card: Type of Design dropdown + "Add New Type," Client Expectation, What to Avoid, Additional Information (rich-text/image-embed, reusing the existing revision-text capability).
- **Deliverables — two distinct modes:** Edit mode (Add Deliverable rows, Apply Deadline to All, Save Deliverables) and Saved mode (clean collapsed read view + "Edit Deliverables" button). Same shared component reused inline on the Detail page.

**Review & Submit modal — redesign locked.** Confirmed field set: Project Basics, Deadlines, Design Teams Required (chips), Type of Design, a Deliverables summary (count, not full detail), a Reference Files count. C&CM version: same modal + selected customers via the same chip-strip.

**Note — still provisional as of 28 Jul 2026:** Ezekiel also has a new idea for this page's redesign. This whole section reflects the 17 Jul 2026 wireframe pass — treat it as the prior baseline, not final, until the new idea is walked through and this doc is updated.

