## Detail Page — Submission Section (in progress, 17 Jul 2026 — provisional, part of the still-unbuilt Detail page)

The **Submissions** rail sub-section within Design. Needs real structural rework, not just a reskin.

- **Exit/undo-branch audit** — see "Universal undo principle" below.
- **Channel switcher — resolved: browser-tab-style, not pills.**
- **Gulf regions get per-customer submission routes, not just per-region.** Each Gulf customer needs its own independent submission route (own Draft, own cards, own revision counters) — same Region → Customer nesting already locked for C&CM Deliverables. **Confirmed likely a pure logic change, not a schema change** — see Code Architecture Section F below.

**Page structure:** two parallel cards — Design Submissions and Technical File Submissions — plus a Submission History card below both. Action Button is context-sensitive ("Upload Submission" / "Start Revision"). Technical files route to their own NAS subfolder, auto-copy to `deliverablefolder/DWG`or `/PDF` on approval. The button formerly "Upload Internal Revision" is renamed **"Inform CS for Internal Review."**

**Core lifecycle model:**
- **Draft vs. sent.** A submission is a mutable draft — files/deliverable selection freely editable — until actually sent. Internal review sendbacks don't touch a revision counter.
- **Only ONE active draft per channel.** CS-facing view capped at max two things: a sent submission needing a decision, and the current open draft.
- **Per-deliverable revision tracking — automatic, system-computed.** "Initial" first appearance, "Revision N" every time after, derived from that deliverable's own submission history.
- **Revision number labeling:** two distinct, clearly-tagged counts — "Deliverable Revision Count" vs. "Project/Customer Revision Count" — never a bare unlabeled number.
- **Internal Review — a soft notify-and-comment layer, not a hard gate.** The draft stays fully editable. The real permanent gate is Submit to Client.
- **Modified-since-notification check:** at Submit to Client, checks (live, via SSE) whether the draft changed since the last "Inform CS" ping.
- **"Start Revision"** just returns to normal Draft editing, no separate re-review gate.
- **Discard entire draft** — low visual weight, confirm-gated.
- **Expected deck filename shown in draft mode** — previews current deck name, or next revision's name if opened via "Start Revision."
- **Project/Customer-level revision counter — separate, manual, CS-confirmed.** At send, CS is asked "Is this submission a revision?" — Yes increments the channel-level counter and renames the deck file; No leaves it untouched.
- **Deck file versioning:** non-revision sends overwrite the same file in place; a confirmed revision creates a new, separately-preserved file.

**Universal undo principle:** every forward transition gets a paired, visible undo/reopen action, all logged to the activity log the same as every other action.

**Undo rights per role:** designers don't need undo (draft is always mutable pre-send). Reserved for CS/Admin/Management: Sent to Client → back to draft; Revision Requested → back to Sent to Client; Approved → actual prior state (asks whether to also clean up already-auto-copied files).

**Deliverable picker + display:** reuses the Deliverables section's own row list as the picker (checkbox-style "select for this submission" mode), filtered by default to non-Approved.

**CS notes on Sent-to-Client and Approved:** optional free-text note field, shown in Submission History.

**Simplified state machine after the audit:** Draft (always editable, optional non-blocking Internal Review ping) → Submit to Client (real permanent gate, with modified-since check) → Sent to Client → [Approved, or Revision Requested → Start Revision reopens Draft, no re-review required]. Technical route mirrors this with "Mark Approved" as its terminal gate.

