## Sitewide Density / Sizing System (locked 17 Jul 2026 — built, kept here for reference)

Every size that should scale with density — font sizes, padding, gaps, avatar diameter, row height — is expressed in `rem` (relative to root `<html>` font-size) rather than hardcoded `px`, so changing one root value proportionally scales the entire app's density at once. **Not** a user-facing density toggle — deliberately out of scope.

This token layer (`main.css`'s `:root` block) is already built and live — reuse it for the Detail and Briefing pages rather than inventing new sizing values. Existing older CSS mixes `rem`/hardcoded `px` inconsistently; new work should have real discipline here.

---

## Build Process / File Organization (locked 17 Jul 2026)

**Fresh files, never edits to the old ones.** Old files (`dashboards/cs.html`/`designer.html`/`team_lead.html` — already replaced; `projects_detail.py` and siblings, `detail.js`, `create.html` — still to come) are read as reference only, to understand existing behavior before porting it. New code always goes into brand-new files. Old files get deleted in the same pass that cuts a new page over.

**Comment standard is non-negotiable and applies across the board** — what/how/why per block, same rule already governing every other file in the app.

**File granularity, decided per page:**
- **Projects page:** done — one blueprint, one template, one JS file, one CSS file. See `Projects.md`.
- **Detail page:** one JS+CSS pair PER DEPARTMENT TAB — `detail-design.js`/`detail-design.css` first (today's entire existing detail-page logic lands here), `detail-finance.*`/`detail-production.*`/`detail-logistics.*` created only when that tab's real content gets built, not pre-stubbed. Replaces today's single monolithic `detail.js`.
- **Briefing page:** single file each for JS/CSS, matching its "visual-overhaul-only" scope.

